{"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:encoder:)","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:transport:encoder:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/Destination-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoding","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPTransport","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13HTTPTransportP","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoding","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations12BatchEncoderP","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The wire shape, for a server that ingests these batches:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One request per batch, in the order the delivery hands them over, the next sent only once"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the previous one has a response or has failed."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The method is ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the URL is the configured endpoint.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The header fields are the configured ones, then the trace context of the batch’s first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record, then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"text":", each replacing fields of the same name before it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The instrument injects the first (oldest) record’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extracting it joins the request, and the events, to the trace the app was in. Its field","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names are the instrument’s: ","type":"text"},{"code":"traceparent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracestate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a W3C Trace Context tracer.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record tracked outside any span, or an instrument that injects nothing (the default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NoOpInstrument","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when none is bootstrapped), adds no fields.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Only the first record’s context travels in the header fields, though a batch may hold","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records tracked in other traces. A server that needs each record’s context reads it from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the body, where a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" writes it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/contentType","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", whatever a configured"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"field or the instrument wrote."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is exactly the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/body","type":"reference"},{"text":" for the batch’s records, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first. The format is the encoder’s; events need no ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A response with a 2xx status means the batch arrived. Any other status, or no response,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"means it didn’t; either way the batch is not sent again."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" handles its own failures: a batch the encoder can’t encode, a send that gets","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no response and a response that isn’t 2xx are each logged at error level and dropped, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the delivery and its other destinations carry on. A cancelled delivery cancels the send in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"flight, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" returns without logging it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder())","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"HTTPDestination.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination.swift#L44"},"modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"HTTPDestination","role":"symbol"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends each batch it receives to an HTTP endpoint, as one request.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/